    "id": "K09",
    "points": 1,
    "description": "Netz- und Systemsicherheit: nur bei richtiger Zuordnung aller drei Vorfälle, konkretem Bezug auf erlaubte/verhinderte Verbindungen und den genannten Grenzen der drei Mechanismen."
  },
  "freshContentReason": [
    "The unchanged target requires classifying TLS, authentication/authorization and firewalls. The new prior competence explicitly supplies authentication, logs and client-server risks; its existing path supplies protocol communication and TCP/IP. It does not already demand success at the complete K09 performance.",
    "C1 supplies the full browser-HTTPS-gateway-service-database diagram, certificate/hostname condition, role check and external/internal firewall rules. V1 interception, V2 an authenticated but unauthorized account and V3 a direct database-port attempt remain concrete and independently answerable.",
    "The actual solution correctly distinguishes channel confidentiality/integrity and server authentication from application authorization and network filtering. It states the limits for compromised endpoints, storage and unencrypted internal links; the necessary internal service-to-database link remains allowed.",
    "K09 still awards its sole point only for all three correct mappings plus the actual allowed/blocked links and limits. A learner cannot replace the missing security competence with unrelated circuit or Prolog points because all19 full binary criteria are mandatory.",
    "Neither these tasks nor the target require binary/hexadecimal arithmetic or two-s-complement calculation. Replacing that unrelated preparation chain with existing network-risk competence leaves the tested security meaning, difficulty and complete proof obligation intact.",
    "The technical-informatics containment label adds no inherited prerequisite. It does not supply a hidden reason to require the removed numeric chain. No new role, coverage ID or learner result is inferred from this review."
  ],
